{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787076421766927485,"compiled_state":{"alias":"fancy-felonious-ant","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ba2ab916a8079ca84b95def14a950f4304b0478b8ec2f63ec043367fca1469e5","event_uuid":"880a3377-7ce1-45df-91ac-e075e1360c60","position":{"commit_sha":"845f0fb09906c0c4ca6ae12f583d913d14cb3670","position":"1787070476629784001-880a3377-7ce1-45df-91ac-e075e1360c60"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"22a26e4349e80539a8cfdd4142d640692b5be1353bd02f731548fc2a342fa111","event_uuid":"1a10e5f1-7618-47bb-892d-00c1f00c6528","position":{"commit_sha":"7695a8f0cfbc75c18aaa9cceda00391156fb2243","position":"1787070549731702001-1a10e5f1-7618-47bb-892d-00c1f00c6528"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"04027fe91503dbd6c348d3c5cb787baca988491832131153f9a57df39fce5cb9","event_uuid":"8f668556-2114-43de-81fd-08cc2f63c832","position":{"commit_sha":"d003932bd173f406f76dafdf6befda8d2667a716","position":"1787070612511596001-8f668556-2114-43de-81fd-08cc2f63c832"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1e75ac97985ba02532d7a8674ceccdd051d4145a0eb463cd8bc7001a16dac90b","event_uuid":"d1a68911-0e99-4b49-ba2a-a5040bbf6cd4","position":{"commit_sha":"bc6d4925ccee8450e152ff7423c4dc3802698f43","position":"1787070654438813001-d1a68911-0e99-4b49-ba2a-a5040bbf6cd4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787070476629784001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1a10e5f1-7618-47bb-892d-00c1f00c6528","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"b2ff-03f7-a223-4900"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nMost core ticket, store, read/write, config, import/export, maintenance, and gate commands parse argv imperatively. Adding docs-only argparse definitions would create the duplicate grammar RP-05 is meant to eliminate.\n\n## Approach\nInventory every registered core grammar owned by `src/rebar/_commands/`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/`, and `src/rebar/_io/`. For each command:\n\n1. Capture current production-path positive, negative, boundary, surplus/missing argument, option-space/equal, global-output, and `--` behavior from existing tests and focused additions.\n2. Move the grammar into a side-effect-free factory using the S2a argparse contract, extracting shared argument-definition helpers where canonical and compatibility forms overlap.\n3. Switch the runtime handler to parse with that same factory in the same change. Keep domain execution and initialization outside the parser module.\n4. Preserve command-specific diagnostic text, stdout/stderr, and exit codes through the shared parser seam; do not accept an option merely because argparse can parse it.\n5. Register the parser reference and prove only the selected parser/handler is resolved during execution.\n\nCover the leaf positional registry, reads/lookups/gates, create/edit/lifecycle, compaction/fsck/doctor/maintenance, config, import/export, metrics, identity-adjacent core store commands, and static reads. Split files only along existing command-family call graphs and respect module-size rules.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nNo help cutover occurs here. Accepted grammar and execution behavior are invariant unless this ticket records and receives approval for a specific delta. A parser family and its handler switch are one revertable unit; no stored data changes.\n\n## Testing\nUse the smallest production path crossing each parser. Pure parser tables may be unit-tested, but public oracles run real CLI subprocesses or existing interface tests and assert return code, exact relevant stream, parsed effect/persisted state, and unchanged state on refusal. Include nearest controls and verify tests run under `make test`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every registered core command runtime calls its S2a parser factory; no parallel imperative grammar remains for that command.\n- [ ] Accepted/rejected argv matrices cover missing/surplus values, space/equal options, `--`, global confirmation/output extraction, and representative malformed input.\n- [ ] Existing persisted effects, no-effect refusals, diagnostics, streams, and exit codes show no unapproved behavior delta.\n- [ ] Parser construction imports no domain executor or optional dependency, and selected execution resolves no unrelated parser/handler.\n- [ ] All touched modules meet module-size/complexity policy and each family can be reverted with its handler switch.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/","reason":"Lean core command-family parser factories and shared argument definitions."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/","reason":"Switch core write/lifecycle/config/store handlers from imperative or inline parsing to shared factories."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/","reason":"Switch read/lookup/gate/validation handlers to shared factories."},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/_cli.py","reason":"Switch import/export runtime parsing to shared factories."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/","reason":"Real CLI core argv, effect, stream, and exit-code parity matrices."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/","reason":"Core command grammar and output contract coverage."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_core_cli_parsers.py","reason":"Pure parser boundary and import-clean tests."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","b2ff-03f7-a223-4900"],["parent","2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp05","cli"],"ticket_id":"eb0d-4c3d-5344-47d7","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-05 S2b — Migrate core command grammars to shared argparse factories","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_core_cli_parsers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_space_form_options.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_leaf_writes_parity.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes_doc_conformance.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC4","dd_text":"Core shared-parser and real CLI argv/effect/stream/exit parity"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"Core parser migration module-size, complexity, lint, and types"}]},"source_event_uuids":["880a3377-7ce1-45df-91ac-e075e1360c60","1a10e5f1-7618-47bb-892d-00c1f00c6528","8f668556-2114-43de-81fd-08cc2f63c832","d1a68911-0e99-4b49-ba2a-a5040bbf6cd4"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787076421766927485,"uuid":"5119eba2-096e-4ec4-b385-c72af283fb74"}